    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493338034/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Monday, Mar. 9, 1908
Warm. Glorious.
Logan. Perkins.
Logan lunched with the Dodges and Miss Fletcher, and I met him at Villa Imperiale and drove with him to call on Sir Thomas Dick Lauder, who showed us some of his collection of book-plates, which I found very interesting.
Mr. Fowler came in, and then Frau von Grunelius from Frankfort. 
Left cards on the Brocklebanks, and called at the Spaldings. Alberto received us, and was very amusing, and awfully nice.Returned to find Perkins here, poor nervous ship-wrecked being.
Our only nephew, Ralph Perry, Rachel’s son 1 1/4 years old. [caption for photo of Ralph and Rachel]"""^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 91 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1908> .

